CORE
gated_clock_operators1.sv
--show-rtl
^\$root\.main\.q1\[0:0\] register, next-state value: main\.en \? main\.d : main\.q1$
^\$root\.main\.q2\[0:0\] register, next-state value: main\.sel \? main\.d : main\.q2$
^\$root\.main\.q4\[0:0\] register, next-state value: main\.sel && main\.en \? main\.d : main\.q4$
^\$root\.main\.q5\[0:0\] register, next-state value: main\.sel && main\.en \? main\.d : main\.q5$
^\$root\.main\.q6\[0:0\] register, next-state value: main\.sel \|\| main\.en \? main\.d : main\.q6$
^\$root\.main\.r\[0:0\] register, next-state value: main\.d$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The gating condition is derived structurally for and, or, xor, not and
the conditional operator, and composes through intermediate nets.
